[00:00.62] Crazy Captain Gunboat Willie
[00:04.16] Growled out his commands
[00:07.08] And all the able seamen
[00:10.00] Clicked their heels and swore
[00:12.32] They would protect the noble ship
[00:15.02] In peace-time and in war
[00:17.14] And they danced a jig until the dawn
[00:20.44] Sang a loyal sailors song
[00:23.12] Drank a pot of steaming rum
[00:25.38] Did all the things that loyal sailors do
[00:31.36] Captain Bill expressed great glee
[00:34.64] All the things that he had planned
[00:37.86] Were made to go his way
[00:40.36] All the fares he had collected and salted away
[00:45.38] Made his lips turn in a smile
[00:48.52] Just then Luke the rat from down below
[00:51.70] Called to Gunboat Bill
[00:54.38] He said
[00:56.10] Listen to those madmen wail
[00:58.40] They've been at sea for ninety days
[01:01.56] Without the sight of land
[01:03.48] No it doesn't look so good to me
[01:06.50] No it doesn't look so good at all
[01:08.78] The captain pondered what the rat had said
[01:11.92] Until he could think of nothing more
[01:14.24] Then he threw his crew into the foaming sea
[01:16.78] At least a thousand miles from shore
[01:19.06] And he danced a jig until the dawn
[01:22.34] Sang a loyal captain's song
[01:25.02] Drank a pot of steaming rum
[01:27.28] Did all the things that loyal captains do
[01:31.94] The rat looked hard at Gunboat Bill
[01:36.54] And he said in a serious style
[01:39.64] As he leapt into the water
[01:42.52] Don't believe, no don't believe
[01:44.92] Don't believe everything that you hear
